into units.amni
use os, math
dialect js

The unit system `SYS` is "si" if the file amnicad.sys holds "si" once trimmed, else "us". `sys` returns it. `set_sys` sets it to "si" for "si" and "us" for anything else, then saves it to that file, ignoring failure.

`doc_units` gives "in" for "in" and "mm" for anything else. `mm_per` gives the millimeters per document unit: 25.4 for inches, 1 for millimeters.

`nf` shows a number with some decimals, by default -1, as a new string. A non-finite number shows "—". With -1, the size of the number picks the decimals: 0 from 1000 up, 1 from 100, 2 from 10, 3 from 1, 4 from 0.01, else 5. The text is `js::fixed_locale` of the number, the decimals and true.

`unit_entry` gives a quantity's label, factor and offset in a system, "si" or "us". An unknown quantity aborts with "unknown quantity". Metric factors are 1 and offsets are 0 unless shown.
quantity | si | factor | us | factor | offset
len | mm | | in | 1/25.4
area | mm² | | in² | 1/645.16
vol | cm³ | 1e-3 | in³ | 1/16387.064
mass | kg | | lb | 2.2046226
force | N | | lbf | 0.22480894
press, stress | MPa | | psi | 145.03774
modulus | GPa | 1e-3 | Msi | 1.4503774e-4
torque | N·mm | | lbf·in | 0.0088507458
temp | °C | | °F | 1.8 | 32
dtemp | K | | °F | 1.8
power | W | | BTU/hr | 3.4121416
film | W/m²K | | BTU/hr·ft²·°F | 0.17611016
cond | W/m·K | | BTU/hr·ft·°F | 0.57782155
speed | m/s | | mph | 2.2369363
dens | kg/m³ | | lb/in³ | 3.6127292e-5
accel | m/s² | | ft/s² | 3.2808399
freq | Hz | | Hz | 1
pa | Pa | | psf | 0.020885434

`conv` turns a metric value into a system's unit: times the factor, plus the offset. `back` undoes it: minus the offset, divided by the factor. `to_si` and `from_si` do the same for the current system. `unit_of` gives the label in a system, by default the current one.

`one` shows a metric value in a system (default current) with some decimals (default -1): the `nf` of the converted value, a space and the label. `dual` shows it in the current system, then the other in parentheses, like `2 in (50.8 mm)`.
